msgstr "nombre"

#: apps/users/models.py:465
msgid "last name"
msgstr "apellidos"

#: apps/users/models.py:467
msgid "role"
msgstr "perfil"

#: apps/users/models.py:469
msgid "staff number"
msgstr "nº de empleado"

#: apps/users/models.py:473
msgid ""
"The person's identifier in the company's own systems. Acts as a bridge when "
"an external application records clock events on their behalf."
msgstr ""
"El identificador de la persona en los sistemas de la propia empresa. Sirve "
"de puente cuando una aplicación externa registra fichajes en su nombre."

#: apps/users/models.py:481
msgid "Overrides the company language for this person."
msgstr "Sustituye el idioma de la empresa para esta persona."

#: apps/users/models.py:493
msgid "working-time regime"
msgstr "régimen de jornada"

#: apps/users/models.py:497
msgid "Art. 3.b. Decides which limits apply, not just how many hours."
msgstr "Art. 3.b. Decide qué límites se aplican, no solo cuántas horas."

#: apps/users/models.py:500
msgid "contracted hours"
msgstr "horas contratadas"

#: apps/users/models.py:506
msgid ""
"The figure the contract agreed. Empty on a full-time contract means the "
"company's own; empty with no agreed figure means there is none."
msgstr ""
"La cifra que pactó el contrato. Vacío en jornada completa significa la de la "
"empresa; vacío sin cifra pactada significa que no la hay."

#: apps/users/models.py:511
msgid "over"
msgstr "sobre"

#: apps/users/models.py:515
msgid "Whether the figure above is a week, a month or a year."
msgstr "Si la cifra anterior es semanal, mensual o anual."

#: apps/users/models.py:524
msgid "contract starts"
msgstr "el contrato empieza"

#: apps/users/models.py:527
msgid "Empty means it was already running when the company started here."
msgstr ""
"Vacío significa que ya estaba en marcha cuando la empresa empezó a usar esto."

#: apps/users/models.py:530
msgid "contract ends"
msgstr "el contrato acaba"

#: apps/users/models.py:533
msgid "Empty means open-ended. A date makes it fixed-term."
msgstr "Vacío significa indefinido. Con fecha, es temporal."

#: apps/users/models.py:552
msgid "relieves"
msgstr "releva a"

#: apps/users/models.py:553
msgid "Art. 12.7: who this relief contract stands in for."
msgstr "Art. 12.7: a quién sustituye este contrato de relevo."

#: apps/users/models.py:557
msgid "permanent seasonal"
msgstr "fijo discontinuo"

#: apps/users/models.py:560
msgid ""
"Art. 16 ET: the work comes in periods of activity. Outside them there is no "
"expected working day, and the roster says so instead of reporting an absence."
msgstr ""
"Art. 16 ET: el trabajo viene por periodos de actividad. Fuera de ellos no "
"hay jornada prevista, y el cuadrante lo dice en vez de contarlo como una "
"ausencia."

#: apps/users/models.py:566
msgid "agreed hours"
msgstr "horario pactado"

#: apps/users/models.py:570
msgid ""
"Art. 3.b: the agreed working hours, as text. For example 'L-V 09:00-17:00'. "
"Free text because a schedule is not a shape a closed field can hold."
msgstr ""
"Art. 3.b: el horario pactado, como texto. Por ejemplo 'L-V 09:00-17:00'. "
"Texto libre porque un horario no tiene una forma que quepa en un campo "
"cerrado."

#: apps/users/models.py:580
msgid "night worker"
msgstr "trabajador nocturno"

#: apps/users/models.py:585
msgid ""
"Art. 36.1 ET. A status, not a shift: three hours of the daily working day at "
"night as a rule, or a third of the year. It brings an eight-hour average "
"over fifteen days and a ban on overtime. Leave it on automatic to read it "
"from the roster."
msgstr ""
"Art. 36.1 ET. Es una condición de la persona, no del turno: normalmente tres "
"horas de la jornada diaria en horario nocturno, o un tercio de la jornada "
"anual. Trae un promedio de ocho horas en quince días y la prohibición de "
"horas extraordinarias. Déjalo en automático para leerlo del cuadrante."

#: apps/users/models.py:592
msgid "rotating shifts"
msgstr "turnos rotativos"

#: apps/users/models.py:595
msgid ""
"Art. 36.3 ET. The person rotates between shift teams. This does not add "
"limits: it stops the ordinary ones being applied to a changeover, where a "
"shorter rest is lawful and owed back rather than a breach."
msgstr ""
"Art. 36.3 ET. La persona rota entre equipos de turno. Esto no añade límites: "
"evita que se apliquen los ordinarios a un relevo, donde un descanso más "
"corto es lícito y se devuelve, no se incumple."

#: apps/users/models.py:601
msgid "volunteered for nights"
msgstr "adscripción voluntaria a noches"

#: apps/users/models.py:604
msgid ""
"Art. 36.3 ET allows more than two consecutive weeks on the night shift only "
"when the person asked for it. Recorded here because the roster cannot tell a "
"volunteer from somebody left there."
msgstr ""
"El art. 36.3 ET permite más de dos semanas consecutivas en el turno de noche "
"solo si la persona lo ha pedido. Se anota aquí porque el cuadrante no "
"distingue a quien se ofrece de a quien dejan ahí."

#: apps/users/models.py:611
msgid "usual mode"
msgstr "modalidad habitual"

#: apps/users/models.py:616
msgid ""
"Art. 3.e. What a clock event assumes when it says nothing; each event can "
"still record the other."
msgstr ""
"Art. 3.e. Lo que asume un fichaje cuando no dice nada; cada uno puede "
"registrar la otra modalidad."

#: apps/users/models.py:622
msgid "date of birth"
msgstr "fecha de nacimiento"

#: apps/users/models.py:626
msgid ""
"Only used to apply the protections the law gives workers under eighteen: "
"eight hours a day, a thirty-minute break from four and a half, two days of "
"weekly rest, and no night work or overtime. Without it those protections "
"cannot be applied, and the system says so rather than assuming the person is "
"an adult."
msgstr ""
"Solo se usa para aplicar las protecciones que la ley da a los menores de "
"dieciocho años: ocho horas diarias, treinta minutos de descanso a partir de "
"cuatro y media, dos días de descanso semanal, y ni trabajo nocturno ni horas "
"extraordinarias. Sin ella no se pueden aplicar, y el sistema lo dice en vez "
"de dar por hecho que la persona es mayor de edad."

#: apps/users/models.py:638
msgid "workers' representative"
msgstr "representante de las personas trabajadoras"

#: apps/users/models.py:641
msgid ""
"Informed when somebody disagrees with a change to their record (art. 4.b), "
"and entitled to consult the register (art. 6.2)."
msgstr ""
"Se le informa cuando alguien discrepa de un cambio en su registro (art. "
"4.b), y tiene derecho a consultar el registro (art. 6.2)."

#: apps/users/models.py:651
msgid "wants clock reminders"
msgstr "quiere recordatorios de fichaje"

#: apps/users/models.py:654
msgid ""
"Send a reminder when a shift starts and there is no entry, or when a day is "
"left open. It prompts the real punch; it never records one."
msgstr ""
"Envía un recordatorio si empieza el turno y no hay entrada, o si queda una "
"jornada abierta. Empuja al fichaje real, nunca registra uno."

#: apps/users/models.py:664
msgid ""
"Overrides the company figure for this person. Empty means the company's. "
"Part-time and mid-year joiners are the usual reason."
msgstr ""
"Sustituye la cifra de la empresa para esta persona. Vacío significa la de la "
"empresa. Lo habitual es la jornada parcial y las altas a mitad de periodo."

#: apps/users/models.py:676
msgid "identity provider subject"
msgstr "identificador en el proveedor de identidad"

#: apps/users/models.py:684
msgid "admin site access"
msgstr "acceso al sitio de administración"

#: apps/users/models.py:685
msgid "date joined"
msgstr "fecha de alta"

#: apps/users/models.py:693
msgid "person"
msgstr "persona"

#: apps/users/models.py:694
msgid "people"
msgstr "personas"

#: apps/users/models.py:976
msgid "activity starts"
msgstr "la actividad empieza"

#: apps/users/models.py:978
msgid "activity ends"
msgstr "la actividad acaba"

#: apps/users/models.py:981
msgid "Empty while the season is open: a campaign knows when it starts."
msgstr ""
"Vacío mientras la temporada siga abierta: una campaña sabe cuándo empieza."

#: apps/users/models.py:984
msgid "called up on"
msgstr "llamamiento el"

#: apps/users/models.py:988
msgid ""
"Art. 16.3 ET: the call-up is in writing and with notice. The date is what "
"shows the notice was given; a tick would not."
msgstr ""
"Art. 16.3 ET: el llamamiento es por escrito y con antelación. La fecha es lo "
"que demuestra que se avisó; una casilla marcada, no."

#: apps/users/models.py:995
msgid "period of activity"
msgstr "periodo de actividad"

#: apps/users/models.py:996
msgid "periods of activity"
msgstr "periodos de actividad"

#: apps/users/models.py:1049
msgid "signed on"
msgstr "firmado el"

#: apps/users/models.py:1050
msgid "Art. 5.1: the agreement comes before the remote work starts."
msgstr "Art. 5.1: el acuerdo va antes de que empiece el trabajo a distancia."

#: apps/users/models.py:1052
msgid "remote work starts"
msgstr "el trabajo a distancia empieza"

#: apps/users/models.py:1054
msgid "remote work ends"
msgstr "el trabajo a distancia acaba"

#: apps/users/models.py:1057
msgid "Empty for an open-ended agreement, which is the usual one."
msgstr "Vacío para un acuerdo sin fecha de fin, que es el corriente."

#: apps/users/models.py:1060
msgid "share agreed (%)"
msgstr "porcentaje pactado (%)"

#: apps/users/models.py:1066
msgid ""
"Art. 7.f asks the agreement to state it. Left empty it is not checked "
"against what is actually worked: the figure that binds is on paper."
msgstr ""
"El art. 7.f pide que el acuerdo lo diga. Vacío no se contrasta con lo que se "
"trabaja de verdad: la cifra que obliga es la del papel."

#: apps/users/models.py:1073
msgid "remote work agreement"
msgstr "acuerdo de trabajo a distancia"

#: apps/users/models.py:1074
msgid "remote work agreements"
msgstr "acuerdos de trabajo a distancia"

#: apps/users/models.py:1110
msgid "In negotiation"
msgstr "En negociación"

#: apps/users/models.py:1111
msgid "Accepted"
msgstr "Aceptada"

#: apps/users/models.py:1112
msgid "An alternative was proposed"
msgstr "Se propuso una alternativa"

#: apps/users/models.py:1113
msgid "Refused"
msgstr "Denegada"

#: apps/users/models.py:1114
msgid "Withdrawn by the person"
msgstr "Retirada por la persona"

#: apps/users/models.py:1152
msgid "requested on"
msgstr "solicitada el"

#: apps/users/models.py:1153
msgid "The fifteen days of art. 34.8 count from here."
msgstr "Los quince días del art. 34.8 se cuentan desde aquí."

#: apps/users/models.py:1156
msgid "what is being asked"
msgstr "qué se pide"

#: apps/users/models.py:1158
msgid ""
"Duration, distribution, or the way the work is done --- remote included."
msgstr ""
"Duración, distribución o forma de prestación ---incluido a distancia---."

#: apps/users/models.py:1166
msgid "answered on"
msgstr "contestada el"

#: apps/users/models.py:1168
msgid "answer"
msgstr "respuesta"

#: apps/users/models.py:1172
msgid ""
"Art. 34.8 asks for this in writing, and for a reason when the answer is not "
"a plain yes."
msgstr ""
"El art. 34.8 lo pide por escrito, y con motivo cuando la respuesta no es un "
"sí a secas."

#: apps/users/models.py:1182
msgid "answered by"
msgstr "contestada por"

#: apps/users/models.py:1186
msgid "schedule adaptation"
msgstr "adaptación de jornada"

#: apps/users/models.py:1187
